{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":40203396,"ns":0,"title":"Material inference","extract":"In logic, inference is the process of deriving logical conclusions from premises known or assumed to be true. In checking a logical inference for formal and material validity, the meaning of only its logical vocabulary and of both its logical and extra-logical vocabulary\nis considered, respectively.","description":"Process in logic","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}